person.prompt:
Research '${label}' as a PERSON, mentioned here: "${context}".

Return a strict JSON object with this format:
{
  "profile": {
    "summary": "1-2 sentence overview of who this person is",
    "current_work": "What they currently do or are best known for now",
    "notable_background": "A concise note about notable prior work, expertise, or context relevant to understanding them"
  },
  "sources": [
    { "title": "...", "url": "...", "description": "...", "type": "wikipedia|official|profile" }
  ]
}

SOURCE PRIORITY:
1. Wikipedia page if one exists
2. Official website, institutional profile, or company bio page
3. LinkedIn or another high-quality profile only if the first two are unavailable

Keep the profile factual, concise, and useful to a listener trying to understand why this person matters in the episode.

